Fixing StyleBro's rules and the built-in rules init and migrate turn on (142 ids); --all applies every analyzer's and compiler fix.
Held back: IDE0049: this .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' ignores the suppressor StyleBro's multi-target guard uses for IDE rules, so their fixes could write C# or APIs that another target framework or project compiling the same file doesn't have. They aren't applied here; a newer .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' applies them where the guard allows.
Multi-targeted: one 'dotnet format' run per target framework (net10.0, net462, net472, netstandard2.0).
Shared files: these projects compile the same files with other '#if' symbols or settings, so each group gets a run of its own (loaded together, 'dotnet format' crashes: https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/issues/86001): log4net-611-main, log4net-672, log4net-673, log4net-681 and 1 more | log4net.Ext.Mail.Tests | log4net.Tests.
